// `#[at_least_one]` on `min`'s declaration, which is part of its *arity* rather than a check in
// front of it -- `ovl_min_arity` reads the attribute, so the set is distinguishable with it. The
// message came from the arm until 2026-10-22 and now comes from the attribute, which is why it
// names the parameter and the escape (an array spreads, and may be empty at the type level even
// though this one would then fail at run time -- min_max_empty_array_rejected is that case).
//
// `min` left the prelude for the `math` module the same day, hence `math.min()` and `use math`.
use math

fn main() {
    print(math.min())
}
